      "content": "9.1 Political Personalities"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Gegong Apang served as one of the longest-tenured Chief Ministers in Indian history, leading Arunachal Pradesh for over 22 years.",
        "Mamang Dai received the Sahitya Akademi Award in 2017 for her renowned novel 'The Black Hill'.",
        "Lummer Dai and Yeshe Dorjee Thongchi are prominent literary icons who significantly enriched Assamese and Arunachali literature.",
        "Anshu Jamsenpa set a world record by becoming the first woman to scale Mount Everest twice in five days.",
        "Tapi Mra made history as the first person from Arunachal Pradesh to successfully summit Mount Everest."
      ],
      "id": "clcmw7v"
